<title>INDONESIA: Former Moroccan premier new OIC chief.</title>
<headline>Former Moroccan premier new OIC chief.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Moroccan prime minister Azeddine Laraki was unanimously elected the new secretary-general of the Organisation of the Islamic Conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>He succeeds Hamid Algabid of Niger, who served two four-year terms as the head of the 54-member organisation. Algabid is currently a candidate for the post of secretary-general of the United Nations.</p>
<p>Laraki's four assistants would be named later through the OIC secretariat in Jeddah, Indonesian Foreign Minister Ali Alatas said.</p>
</text>
